The files here are generated, not hand-written: the `driver` actions of every
illumos-gate usr/src/pkg/manifests/*.p5m at the pinned gate rev ac45d71f
(gate-drivers.txt, one action per line) rendered into the /etc driver database
format that pkg(5) would write on install. The gate proto itself ships only a
4-entry name_to_major, so before this the database was copied from the build host.
Majors: the gate proto's own 4 entries keep their numbers, the rest are assigned in
manifest order.

etc-var-attrs.tsv (gen-etc-var-attrs.sh <gate checkout>) is the owner, group and
mode of every etc/ and var/ dir and file in the same manifests, with the
transforms/defaults defaults (root, bin, 0644/0755). install-be applies it to the
stock /etc and /var it lays into a BE, as pkg(5) would: the store keeps no owners,
and daemons that drop privilege (dlmgmtd as dladm, ipmgmtd as netadm) cannot write
their state into a root-owned tree.

Local additions to gate-drivers.txt (not in the gate manifests; regenerate with
`python3 gen.py`, which reproduces the committed files byte for byte):
  usbecm alias=usbbda,8153.2  Realtek RTL8153 USB gigabit adapters in their
      standard CDC-ECM configuration (config value 2). That configuration splits
      control and data across two interfaces with no interface association, so
      usbecm must own the whole device: bound per interface, usb_set_alt_if on
      the data interface returns USB_INVALID_PERM (usbai_util.c). The ".2" suffix
      is the usbVID,PID.configCN compatible name (usba.c), so config 1 (vendor,
      Linux r8152 only) never matches. Same whole-device binding as the Sun SP
      alias usb430,a4a2. Pairs with /etc/usb/config_map.conf (configurations/
      base.nix), which makes illumos select config 2.
